  "text": "{\n  \"issues\": [\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"contradiction\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"description\": \"Plan line 188 claims that when the active tab is closed or releases its lock, waiting tabs will automatically take over the lock and re-read storage to initialize the screen. This contradicts Plan line 110 and constraint:5, which explicitly require other tabs to be manually refreshed after closing the active tab ('사용 탭 종료 뒤 새로고침하여 최신 데이터로 시작한다').\",\n      \"suggestedDirection\": \"Align Plan line 188 with Plan line 110 and constraint:5 by specifying that non-holding tabs remain read-only and require manual page refresh after the active tab is closed, rather than performing automatic background lock handoff and re-initialization.\",\n      \"relatedRequirementId\": \"R-6\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"omission\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"description\": \"Constraint:3 requires that storage read exceptions preserve data without writes, alert the user, and block modifications ('읽기 예외도 쓰기 없이 안내·변경 차단한다'). While Plan lines 103-107 specify behavior for null, empty strings, and malformed JSON payloads, they omit handling for exceptions thrown during storage reading (such as SecurityError or DOMException on storage access).\",\n      \"suggestedDirection\": \"Update Section R-6 (Plan lines 103-107) to explicitly specify that any read exception thrown when accessing localStorage preserves existing data, displays an error notice, and blocks all write operations without overwriting.\",\n      \"relatedRequirementId\": \"R-6\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"questions\": [],\n  \"storageAudit\": {\n    \"format\": \"json\",\n    \"evidenceLines\": [135, 137, 138, 159, 178, 179],\n    \"rationale\": \"Plan defines persistent data as a single JSON object stored in localStorage under the key 'EXPENSE_TRACKER_STORE' containing schemaVersion, nextSeq, and records array.\",\n    \"cases\": [\n      {\n        \"state\": \"absent\",\n        \"action\": \"initialize\",\n        \"verdict\": \"consistent\",\n        \"evidenceLines\": [12, 104],\n        \"authorizationScopeIds\": [\"constraint:3\"],\n        \"rationale\": \"Plan line 104 strictly treats null (key absent) as the sole normal initial run condition and initializes the default schema structure.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"state\": \"present_empty\",\n        \"action\": \"preserve_and_block\",\n        \"verdict\": \"consistent\",\n        \"evidenceLines\": [105, 106, 107, 112],\n        \"authorizationScopeIds\": [\"constraint:3\"],\n        \"rationale\": \"Plan lines 105-107 and 112 explicitly treat empty strings and whitespace as integrity violations, preserving original data and blocking all write operations without reset.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"state\": \"invalid\",\n        \"action\": \"preserve_and_block\",\n        \"verdict\": \"consistent\",\n        \"evidenceLines\": [34, 105, 106, 107],\n        \"authorizationScopeIds\": [\"constraint:3\"],\n        \"rationale\": \"Plan lines 105-107 preserve malformed JSON, unknown schema versions, and schema/value violations in place while blocking all writes.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"state\": \"valid\",\n        \"action\": \"load\",\n        \"verdict\": \"consistent\",\n        \"evidenceLines\": [101, 102],\n        \"authorizationScopeIds\": [\"requirement:R-6\"],\n        \"",
